#X connect 24 1 26 0;
#X connect 24 0 25 0;
#X connect 27 0 22 1;
#X obj 140 435 spigot;
#X obj 300 400 r \$0-own;
#X obj 900 435 spigot;
#X obj 1060 400 r \$0-own;
#X connect 3 0 31 0;
#X connect 31 0 4 0;
#X connect 13 0 33 0;
#X connect 33 0 14 0;
#X connect 32 0 31 1;
#X connect 34 0 33 1;
#X restore 20 1000 pd input;
#X text 250 1004 pads and the function ring -- named controls out on param and disp, f 50;
#N canvas 30 30 1600 1100 pressure 0;
#X text 20 20 POLYPHONIC AFTERTOUCH -- per pad \, simultaneous \, and the most expressive control on the rig. It must be enabled on the DEVICE and is not the default: hold Setup \, press the third Track Select button \, choose Polyphonic Aftertouch. The default is Channel Pressure \, one value for the whole surface \, which looks like a working decode reporting the wrong pad., f 58;
#X text 700 20 THE TRAP THIS FILE EXISTS TO AVOID. polytouchin emits the NOTE BEFORE THE VALUE \, so wiring it straight through lights a pad with the PREVIOUS event's pressure. Here the note goes to a COLD store and the value is what triggers -- the same shape ctlin needs \, for the same reason. It is written down in ref/device/launchpad.md because it has already cost time once., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 polytouchin;
#X obj 140 440 spigot;
#X obj 140 510 t f b;
#X obj 400 580 f;
#X obj 400 640 makefilename pad-%d-at;
#X obj 400 700 s \$0-at-name;
#X obj 700 360 - \$1;
#X obj 700 410 == 0;
#X obj 700 460 s \$0-lp-on;
#X obj 160 350 r \$0-lp-on;
#X obj 20 780 list prepend;
#X obj 20 840 list trim;
#X obj 20 900 s param;
#X obj 700 720 r \$0-at-name;
#X text 20 960 PARAM ONLY \, AND NEVER disp -- A DELIBERATE BREAK WITH m_nano. Every other m_ layer publishes to both off one t a a \, action first and report second. Pressure cannot: it is a continuous stream PER HELD PAD \, so a chord of four fingers would fill the OLED's five param rows and refuse everything else on the bus for as long as they were down. A control that can flood the display does not get to ask for it. What the pressure MEANS is still u_map's business \, and u_map listens on param., f 90;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 2 1 5 1;
#X connect 2 2 8 0;
#X connect 4 1 5 0;
#X connect 4 0 12 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 11 0 3 1;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 15 0 12 1;
#X obj 140 475 spigot;
#X obj 300 440 r \$0-own;
#X connect 3 0 17 0;
#X connect 17 0 4 0;
#X connect 18 0 17 1;
#X restore 20 1100 pd pressure;
#X text 250 1104 polyphonic aftertouch -- param only, f 50;
#X obj 1400 900 r \$0-own;
#X obj 1400 960 outlet;
#N canvas 40 40 2600 1800 watchdog 0;
#X text 20 20 THE REPLUG WATCHDOG. Unplug the Launchpad mid-set and it comes back in LIVE MODE while this file still believes it owns the surface -- so pads send musical pitches \, get decoded as r*10+c \, and publish nonsense to param. Reproduced on both machines. TWO MECHANISMS \, BECAUSE THE TWO PLATFORMS FAIL DIFFERENTLY AND ONE DETECTOR CANNOT COVER BOTH., f 110;
#X text 20 260 MAC: the device answers a universal device inquiry whether it is in Programmer OR Live Mode \, so polling CANNOT detect a Mac replug at all. The HEARTBEAT fixes it instead -- re-asserting Programmer Mode every two seconds needs no detection \, and LED state survives the switch. DEVICE: the replug destroys the ALSA subscriptions outright \, so nothing reaches the device until wire.sh runs again. There the POLL detects loss and a BOUNDED recovery re-wires it., f 110;
#X obj 20 500 r \$0-want;
#X obj 20 560 metro 2000;
#X obj 20 620 t b b b;
#X msg 500 700 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 14 \, 1 \, 247;
#X msg 1000 700 240 \, 126 \, 127 \, 6 \, 1 \, 247;
#X obj 500 780 midiout;
#X obj 1450 620 loadbang;
#X obj 1450 680 f \$1;
#X obj 20 700 f;
#X obj 200 760 + 1;
#X obj 20 820 t f f;
#X obj 20 880 moses 3;
#X obj 20 940 t b b;
#X msg 20 1000 1;
#X obj 20 1060 s \$0-own;
#X msg 220 1000 0;
#X obj 500 940 spigot;
#X obj 500 1000 t b b;
#X msg 500 1060 0;
#X obj 500 1120 s \$0-own;
#X obj 1900 500 sysexin;
#X obj 1900 560 t b b;
#X msg 1900 620 0;
#X obj 1900 680 s \$0-miss-zero;
#X msg 2150 620 1;
#X obj 2150 680 s \$0-armed;
#X obj 700 880 r \$0-armed;
#X obj 700 500 r \$0-miss-zero;
#X obj 1000 1240 f;
#X obj 1200 1300 + 1;
#X obj 1000 1360 t f f f;
#X obj 1000 1420 moses 33;
#X obj 1000 1480 mod 4;
#X obj 1000 1540 sel 0;
#X msg 1000 1600 sh wire.sh;
#X obj 1000 1660 shell;
#X obj 1500 1420 sel 33;
#X msg 1500 1480 fail m_launchpad grid-lost;
#X obj 1500 1540 s err;
#X text 20 1180 THREE MISSED POLLS IS SIX SECONDS \, not one -- a single dropped reply must not blank the grid. moses 3 needs no edge detection: every tick simply re-states ownership \, and g_grid's change -1 makes a repeated 1 free., f 60;
#X text 1900 780 ANY SysEx AT ALL COUNTS AS PRESENCE. Only the Launchpad transmits SysEx in this rig -- measured \, the nanoKONTROL never does -- so matching the Novation ID would buy nothing and cost a byte matcher., f 60;
#X text 1900 1240 THE RECOVERY IS BOUNDED \, and the bound is why this is allowed to exist at all. shell FORKS Pd \, and Phase 4's rule is one fork per load and NEVER per event -- written against error logging \, which cascades without limit. This cannot cascade: the counter ticks every 2 s while the grid is lost \, mod 4 fires wire.sh every FOURTH tick \, and moses 33 stops it dead after eight attempts. First try about 14 s after the cable goes \, last about 70 s \, then it gives up and says so on err rather than forking all night behind a device nobody intends to plug back in. ⚠️ THE FIRST VERSION GAVE UP AFTER 12 SECONDS AND THAT WAS USELESS -- nobody reseats a cable that fast \, and the very first hardware test missed the window. wire.sh costs 133 ms and is idempotent \, and ten forks fired back to back produced no audio complaint on Pd's console -- all measured., f 60;
#X text 20 1420 THE SPIGOT IS THE ARMING GATE \, AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. Ownership can only be DROPPED once a reply has actually been seen \, so a detector that has never once proven it works is never allowed to blank the grid. Without it the headless assert layer -- which has no Launchpad and no sysexin -- lost every frame six seconds in \, and so would any platform where sysexin is missing. It failed 7 of 24 checks and that is how this was found., f 60;
